{"id": "b2b4eaa7-c866-45f9-8dc8-75382d59112a", "slug": "vertexa-build-beyond-the-ordinary", "title": "Vertexa - Build Beyond the Ordinary", "description": "Vertexa Build Onboarding Section is designed for building reusable UI components in modern web projects. Key features include reusable structure, responsive behavior, and production-ready presentation. It is suitable for component libraries and responsive product interfaces.", "content": "---\nversion: \"neuform-staff-featured-2026-05-22\"\nname: \"Vertexa - Build Beyond the Ordinary\"\ndescription: \"Vertexa Build Onboarding Section is designed for building reusable UI components in modern web projects. Key features include reusable structure, responsive behavior, and production-ready presentation. It is suitable for component libraries and responsive product interfaces.\"\ncolors:\n  primary: \"#1845F5\"\n  secondary: \"#000000\"\n  accent: \"#2B52FF\"\n  background: \"#020205\"\n  surface: \"#18181B\"\n  text-primary: \"#FFFFFF\"\n  text-secondary: \"#A1A1AA\"\n  border: \"#27272A\"\ntypography:\n  display-lg:\n    fontFamily: \"Inter\"\n    fontSize: \"64px\"\n    fontWeight: 500\n    lineHeight: \"1.04\"\n    letterSpacing: \"0\"\n  body-md:\n    fontFamily: \"Inter\"\n    fontSize: \"16px\"\n    fontWeight: 400\n    lineHeight: \"1.6\"\n  label-md:\n    fontFamily: \"JetBrains Mono\"\n    fontSize: \"12px\"\n    fontWeight: 600\n    lineHeight: \"1.2\"\nspacing:\n  base: \"8px\"\n  gap: \"16px\"\n  card-padding: \"24px\"\n  section-padding: \"80px\"\nrounded:\n  card: \"8px\"\n  control: \"8px\"\n  pill: \"9999px\"\ncomponents:\n  card:\n    background: \"Use the surface token with subtle borders and HTML-matched shadow depth\"\n    radius: \"Match the declared card radius token\"\n  button:\n    background: \"Use primary or accent colors for the main action\"\n    radius: \"Use the control or pill radius based on the source HTML\"\n---\n# Vertexa - Build Beyond the Ordinary\nSource: Neuform staff featured templates. Author: Sourasith Phomhome (@madebysourasith). Views: 143; favorites: 7; remixes: 2.\nTags: cta, animated, webgl, threejs, dither, navigation, links, support.\n## Overview\nVertexa Build Onboarding Section is designed for building reusable UI components in modern web projects. Key features include reusable structure, responsive behavior, and production-ready presentation. It is suitable for component libraries and responsive product interfaces.\n\nVertexa Products Solutions Resources Company Get Started Build Beyond the Ordinary. We build scalable digital products and experiences that help ambitious companies grow faster. Get Started\n## Composition\nUse the attached HTML reference as the source of truth. Preserve the visible hierarchy, first-screen composition, section rhythm, density, and interaction tone before adapting copy or content.\nFollow the rendered preview for headline scale, supporting copy, navigation density, and component placement.\n## Colors\nAnchor the palette in primary #1845F5, secondary #000000, accent #2B52FF, background #020205, surface #18181B, text-primary #FFFFFF. Keep background, surface, text, and border roles distinct so generated layouts retain the same contrast pattern as the source.\n## Typography\nUse Inter for display moments and Inter for body copy unless the HTML clearly demands a compatible fallback. Labels and technical metadata should use JetBrains Mono or an equivalent mono face.\n## Layout\nKeep spacing deliberate and stable. Favor the same grid direction, max-width behavior, card density, and responsive stacking seen in the HTML. Do not replace distinctive source structures with generic SaaS sections.\n## Components\nAuthentication and CTA controls should preserve the source button hierarchy, input density, and focused conversion path.\n## Motion\nPreserve existing motion cues such as masked reveals, staggered entrance, hover lift, scroll-triggered transitions, and ambient movement. Keep easing smooth and restrained.\n## WebGL & Effects\n\nIf the source includes canvas, WebGL, Three.js, gradients, particles, or atmospheric effects, rebuild them as supporting layers behind the content. Keep effects performant, responsive, and secondary to the interface.\n\n## Guardrails\n- Do not flatten the source into a generic card grid.\n- Do not swap the color mode unless the source clearly supports it.\n- Preserve the first viewport signal, focal object, and visual density.\n- Keep buttons, cards, and badges aligned to the same radius and border language.", "preview_html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Vertexa - Build Beyond the Ordinary</title>\n\n    <!-- Fonts -->\n    <link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\">\n    <link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\" crossorigin>\n    <link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;600&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n\n    <!-- Tailwind CSS -->\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.tailwindcss.com\"></script>\n\n    <!-- Iconify -->\n    <script src=\"https://code.iconify.design/iconify-icon/1.0.7/iconify-icon.min.js\"></script>\n\n    <!-- GSAP & ScrollTrigger -->\n    <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/gsap/3.12.2/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/gsap/3.12.2/ScrollTrigger.min.js\"></script>\n\n    <!-- Three.js for WebGL Animation -->\n    <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/three.js/r128/three.min.js\"></script>\n</head>\n<body class=\"bg-[#020205] text-white font-sans selection:bg-blue-600/30 selection:text-white min-h-screen relative overflow-x-hidden antialiased\" style=\"font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;\">\n\n    <!-- WebGL Background Canvas Container -->\n    <div id=\"canvas-container\" class=\"absolute inset-0 z-0 pointer-events-none opacity-90\"></div>\n\n    <!-- CRT Scanline Overlay -->\n    <div class=\"absolute inset-0 z-0 pointer-events-none mix-blend-overlay opacity-50\" style=\"background: repeating-linear-gradient(0deg, transparent, transparent 2px, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4) 2px, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4) 4px);\"></div>\n\n    <!-- Navigation -->\n    <nav class=\"relative z-20 w-full flex items-center justify-between py-6 px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-20\">\n        <!-- Logo -->\n        <a href=\"#\" class=\"flex items-center gap-2 group\">\n            <svg width=\"28\" height=\"28\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"transform group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-300\">\n                <path d=\"M12 21L2 5H7L12 14L17 5H22L12 21Z\" fill=\"#1845F5\" class=\"opacity-90\"/>\n                <path d=\"M12 21L7 12L12 3L17 12L12 21Z\" fill=\"#3B82F6\" class=\"mix-blend-screen opacity-60\"/>\n            </svg>\n            <span class=\"text-xl font-medium tracking-tight\">Vertexa</span>\n        </a>\n\n        <!-- Desktop Links -->\n        <div class=\"hidden md:flex items-center gap-8 lg:gap-12 absolute left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2\">\n            <a href=\"#\" class=\"text-sm font-light text-gray-300 hover:text-white transition-colors duration-200\">Products</a>\n            <a href=\"#\" class=\"text-sm font-light text-gray-300 hover:text-white transition-colors duration-200\">Solutions</a>\n            <a href=\"#\" class=\"text-sm font-light text-gray-300 hover:text-white transition-colors duration-200\">Resources</a>\n            <a href=\"#\" class=\"text-sm font-light text-gray-300 hover:text-white transition-colors duration-200\">Company</a>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Nav CTA -->\n        <a href=\"#\" class=\"hidden sm:inline-flex items-center justify-center px-5 py-2 text-sm font-light border border-[#1845F5]/60 rounded-lg hover:bg-[#1845F5]/10 hover:border-[#1845F5] transition-all duration-300\">\n            Get Started\n        </a>\n    </nav>\n\n    <!-- Main Hero Section -->\n    <main class=\"relative z-10 flex flex-col justify-center min-h-[85vh] px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-20 max-w-4xl pt-10 pb-20\">\n\n        <!-- Animated Headline -->\n        <div id=\"hero-headline\" class=\"text-5xl sm:text-6xl md:text-7xl lg:text-8xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white leading-[1.05] mb-6 flex flex-col gap-2\">\n            <div class=\"flex flex-wrap gap-x-3 md:gap-x-5\">\n                <span style=\"overflow: hidden; display: inline-block;\">\n                    <span class=\"word-reveal inline-block\" style=\"transform: translateY(110%);\">Build</span>\n                </span>\n                <span style=\"overflow: hidden; display: inline-block;\">\n                    <span class=\"word-reveal inline-block\" style=\"transform: translateY(110%);\">Beyond</span>\n                </span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"flex flex-wrap gap-x-3 md:gap-x-5\">\n                <span style=\"overflow: hidden; display: inline-block;\">\n                    <span class=\"word-reveal inline-block\" style=\"transform: translateY(110%);\">the</span>\n                </span>\n                <span style=\"overflow: hidden; display: inline-block;\">\n                    <span class=\"word-reveal inline-block text-[#2B52FF]\" style=\"transform: translateY(110%);\">Ordinary.</span>\n                </span>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Subheadline -->\n        <p id=\"hero-subtext\" class=\"text-base md:text-lg font-light text-gray-400 max-w-lg mb-10 leading-relaxed opacity-0\" style=\"transform: translateY(20px);\">\n            We build scalable digital products and experiences that help ambitious companies grow faster.\n        </p>\n\n        <!-- CTA Button -->\n        <div id=\"hero-cta\" class=\"opacity-0\" style=\"transform: translateY(20px);\">\n            <a href=\"#\" class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 px-6 py-3.5 bg-[#1845F5] hover:bg-[#153BCC] text-white text-base font-medium rounded-lg transition-all duration-300 group shadow-[0_0_20px_rgba(24,69,245,0.3)] hover:shadow-[0_0_30px_rgba(24,69,245,0.5)]\">\n                Get Started\n                <iconify-icon icon=\"solar:arrow-right-up-linear\" class=\"text-xl transform group-hover:translate-x-0.5 group-hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-transform duration-300\" style=\"stroke-width: 1.5;\"></iconify-icon>\n            </a>\n        </div>\n\n    </main>\n\n    <!-- Scripts -->\n    <script>\n        // --- GSAP Animations ---\n        gsap.registerPlugin(ScrollTrigger);\n\n        // Masked Staggered Word Reveal\n        gsap.to(\".word-reveal\", {\n            y: \"0%\",\n            duration: 1.2,\n            stagger: 0.15,\n            ease: \"power4.out\",\n            delay: 0.2,\n            scrollTrigger: {\n                trigger: \"#hero-headline\",\n                start: \"top 85%\",\n            }\n        });\n\n        // Fade up subtext and CTA\n        gsap.to([\"#hero-subtext\", \"#hero-cta\"], {\n            opacity: 1,\n            y: 0,\n            duration: 1,\n            stagger: 0.2,\n            ease: \"power3.out\",\n            delay: 0.8,\n            scrollTrigger: {\n                trigger: \"#hero-headline\",\n                start: \"top 85%\",\n            }\n        });\n\n        // --- Three.js WebGL Pixel Wave Background ---\n        const initWebGL = () => {\n            const container = document.getElementById('canvas-container');\n            const scene = new THREE.Scene();\n\n            // Use Orthographic camera for 2D screen-space shader effect\n            const camera = new THREE.OrthographicCamera(-1, 1, 1, -1, 0, 1);\n            const renderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({ alpha: true, antialias: false });\n\n            renderer.setSize(window.innerWidth, window.innerHeight);\n            renderer.setPixelRatio(Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio, 2));\n            container.appendChild(renderer.domElement);\n\n            // Shader Material setup\n            const uniforms = {\n                uTime: { value: 0.0 },\n                uResolution: { value: new THREE.Vector2(window.innerWidth, window.innerHeight) }\n            };\n\n            const vertexShader = `\n                varying vec2 vUv;\n                void main() {\n                    vUv = uv;\n                    gl_Position = vec4(position, 1.0);\n                }\n            `;\n\n            const fragmentShader = `\n                varying vec2 vUv;\n                uniform float uTime;\n                uniform vec2 uResolution;\n\n                // Pseudo-random noise functions\n                float random(vec2 st) {\n                    return fract(sin(dot(st.xy, vec2(12.9898,78.233))) * 43758.5453123);\n                }\n\n                float noise(vec2 st) {\n                    vec2 i = floor(st);\n                    vec2 f = fract(st);\n                    float a = random(i);\n                    float b = random(i + vec2(1.0, 0.0));\n                    float c = random(i + vec2(0.0, 1.0));\n                    float d = random(i + vec2(1.0, 1.0));\n                    vec2 u = f * f * (3.0 - 2.0 * f);\n                    return mix(a, b, u.x) + (c - a)* u.y * (1.0 - u.x) + (d - b) * u.x * u.y;\n                }\n\n                void main() {\n                    // Setup grid\n                    vec2 uv = gl_FragCoord.xy / uResolution.xy;\n                    float aspect = uResolution.x / uResolution.y;\n\n                    // Grid resolution (number of blocks across screen)\n                    // Adjust block size based on screen width to keep them relatively uniform\n                    float cols = uResolution.x < 768.0 ? 30.0 : 60.0;\n                    float rows = cols / aspect;\n\n                    // Current cell coordinate\n                    vec2 cell = floor(uv * vec2(cols, rows));\n                    vec2 cellUv = cell / vec2(cols, rows);\n\n                    // Generate ascending terrain shape (wave)\n                    // Base exponential curve rising to the right\n                    float baseSlope = pow(cellUv.x, 2.5) * 0.9;\n\n                    // Add low frequency noise for macroscopic hills/valleys\n                    float macroNoise = (noise(vec2(cellUv.x * 2.0, 0.0)) - 0.5) * 0.4;\n\n                    // Combine and quantize to lock to rows (blocky staircase effect)\n                    float terrainHeight = baseSlope + macroNoise;\n                    terrainHeight = floor(terrainHeight * rows) / rows;\n\n                    // Determine if current pixel is part of a block\n                    // 1. Solid blocks below the terrain line\n                    float isBaseBlock = step(cellUv.y, terrainHeight);\n\n                    // 2. Floating \"glitch\" blocks just above the terrain\n                    float glitchProbability = noise(cell * 0.8 + uTime * 0.5);\n                    // Only appear above terrain and below top screen\n                    float isGlitchZone = step(terrainHeight, cellUv.y) * step(cellUv.y, terrainHeight + 0.4);\n                    // Sparse glitches concentrated on the right side\n                    float isGlitch = step(0.92, glitchProbability) * isGlitchZone * smoothstep(0.2, 1.0, cellUv.x);\n\n                    float activeCell = max(isBaseBlock, isGlitch);\n\n                    // Restrict the whole effect to mostly the right side and bottom\n                    // Create a diagonal fade from top-left to bottom-right\n                    float globalMask = smoothstep(-0.2, 0.8, (cellUv.x - cellUv.y * 0.5));\n                    activeCell *= step(0.5, globalMask + noise(cell)*0.5); // Add noise to edge\n\n                    // Color Setup\n                    // Base color: Deep vibrant blue\n                    vec3 blueColor = vec3(0.05, 0.2, 1.0);\n\n                    // Variation: Some blocks are brighter, pulsing\n                    float pulse = noise(cell * 0.2 + uTime * 0.8);\n                    vec3 highlightColor = vec3(0.2, 0.5, 1.0) * step(0.7, pulse);\n\n                    vec3 cellColor = blueColor + highlightColor;\n\n                    // Dim or turn off some blocks randomly (flicker)\n                    float flicker = step(0.15, noise(cell * 3.0 - uTime * 2.0));\n                    activeCell *= flicker;\n\n                    // Draw borders (gaps between blocks)\n                    vec2 localUv = fract(uv * vec2(cols, rows));\n                    // 5% gap on all sides\n                    float borderMask = step(0.05, localUv.x) * step(0.05, localUv.y) * step(localUv.x, 0.95) * step(localUv.y, 0.95);\n\n                    vec3 finalColor = cellColor * activeCell * borderMask;\n\n                    // Output\n                    gl_FragColor = vec4(finalColor, finalColor.b > 0.1 ? 1.0 : 0.0);\n                }\n            `;\n\n            const material = new THREE.ShaderMaterial({\n                vertexShader,\n                fragmentShader,\n                uniforms,\n                transparent: true\n            });\n\n            const geometry = new THREE.PlaneGeometry(2, 2);\n            const mesh = new THREE.Mesh(geometry, material);\n            scene.add(mesh);\n\n            // Animation Loop\n            const clock = new THREE.Clock();\n            const animate = () => {\n                requestAnimationFrame(animate);\n                uniforms.uTime.value = clock.getElapsedTime();\n                renderer.render(scene, camera);\n            };\n\n            animate();\n\n            // Handle Resize\n            window.addEventListener('resize', () => {\n                const width = window.innerWidth;\n                const height = window.innerHeight;\n                renderer.setSize(width, height);\n                uniforms.uResolution.value.set(width, height);\n            });\n        };\n\n        // Initialize WebGL after DOM is ready\n        document.addEventListener(\"DOMContentLoaded\", initWebGL);\n\n    </script>\n</body>\n</html>", "preview_file_name": "vertexa-build-beyond-the-ordinary.html", "thumbnail_url": "https://hoirqrkdgbmvpwutwuwj.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/design-system-thumbnails/staff-featured-2026-05-22/vertexa-build-beyond-the-ordinary.jpg", "source_name": "vertexa-build-beyond-the-ordinary-DESIGN.md", "views": 252, "forks": 7, "private": false, "featured": true, "created_by": "5bd6211c-bd4c-467c-b442-4312cac4712c", "created_at": "2026-05-22T07:58:12.433844+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-07-02T11:23:44.921422+00:00"}